Dear Iven,

Thank you for your message, and for letting the contractor in today at 16 Brindlewick Mews. The contractor saw moisture at a pipe joint above the kitchen ceiling hatch. The hatch opening is too small to reach it safely, so a limited opening in the ceiling lining may be needed before the joint can be repaired.

No repair has been arranged yet. We have asked the contractor for a full quote and the earliest date he could do the work. Once we have it, we will send it to the landlord for approval. I cannot give you a repair date until the landlord has approved, but I will tell you as soon as there is an answer. Thank you for leaving the hatch closed. Please do not open up the ceiling yourself.

If the dripping returns, you see water near any electrical fitting, or the ceiling begins to sag, please tell us straight away.

Kind regards,
